---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';
import { getActiveGames, getGameUrl } from '@/utils/content';

const games = await getActiveGames();
---

<PageLayout
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`Who writes ${SITE.name}, how the guides are checked, and which games are covered.`}
  intro="Hey, I’m Emir. I make the guides on this site."
>
  <p>
    I started {SITE.name} because I kept running into the same problem: you get stuck in a game, search for the answer,
    and end up scrolling through a 20-minute video or a page full of filler. Here, every guide starts with the short
    answer, then explains the details if you want them.
  </p>

  <h2>How the guides are made</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>ROB RUN:</strong> I’ve put 100+ hours into it, so these guides come from actually playing: robbing stores,
      building bases and getting raided.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GTA 6:</strong> the game is brand new, so these guides are researched from gameplay footage and only
      include facts confirmed by at least two independent sources.
    </li>
    <li>Everything is written in my own words. Nothing is copied from other sites.</li>
    <li>Every guide shows when it was last updated. When a patch changes something, I update the guide.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>
    Games change fast, and I’d rather fix a wrong tip than leave it up. <a href="/contact">Send me a message</a> with
    the guide and what’s wrong, and I’ll check it.
  </p>

  <h2>Games covered</h2>
  {
    games.length > 0 ? (
      <ul>
        {games.map((game) => (
          <li>
            <a href={getGameUrl(game)}>{game.data.name} guides</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <p>The first guides are on the way.</p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is an independent fan site. It’s not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any game developer or
    publisher. Game names and trademarks belong to their owners.
  </p>
  <p>
    The pictures on the game tiles are original illustrations made for this site. They aren’t in-game screenshots or
    official artwork.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
